Security is mandatory.

Implement:

- Secure OAuth authorization.
- State parameter validation.
- PKCE wherever supported by the relevant authorization flow.
- Secure token storage on Windows.
- Token refresh handling.
- Token revocation and disconnection.
- No credentials in logs.
- No credentials in frontend localStorage.
- No hardcoded API secrets.
- No unrestricted filesystem access.
- No arbitrary remote URL fetching.
- No SSRF.
- Strict upload file validation.
- Safe temporary-file cleanup.
- Upload size and duration checks.
- Duplicate submission prevention.
- Explicit publishing confirmation.
- Platform API error handling.
- Secure handling of short-lived media URLs.

Use Windows Credential Manager or an appropriate Windows secure credential-storage mechanism for OAuth credentials where feasible.

Never treat a connected social account as permission to publish every available video automatically.

Never auto-publish without user confirmation.

